Q: How to set the containers height in the css file code? A: <p>wrap the  all 3 containers in one parent container and add margin from the top  or add padding from the top</p>
<p>like this</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;top-left-group&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;Box 1&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;Box 2&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;Box 3&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>then add  margin from the top f the containers use position: absolute</p>
<p>make it relative</p>
<pre><code>.top-left-group {
  margin-top: 80px; 
}
</code></pre>
<p>And by using flex box  You want the two right containers to match the <strong>Rainfall container height.</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;bottom-containers&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;rainfall&quot;&gt;Rainfall&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;humidity&quot;&gt;Humidity&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;wind&quot;&gt;Wind&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>.bottom-containers {
  display: flex;
  align-items: stretch; 
  gap: 16px;
}

.bottom-containers &gt; div {
  flex: 1;
}
</code></pre>
